From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000041
Subject: [PATCH] mod_channel: mods talk to their client plugin over their own packets

Server extension mod_channel (off by default). CZ 0x0cfe / ZC 0x0cff carry a
channel name, a request id and typed values (numbers, strings, arrays).
modchannel binds a channel to an NPC label, which runs as soon as the packet
arrives, also while the player has an NPC dialog open (stock atcommand events
are queued by name only, two at most, until the dialog closes). modsend /
modsendto answer, modready tells whether a client can be sent to. The logic is
in src/map/mod_channel.cpp; this adds the hooks: the packet, the session's
hello and rate counters, an event lookup, and the script commands.

--- a/db/extension_db.yml
+++ b/db/extension_db.yml
@@ -167,6 +167,38 @@
       setstylistcost warns and does nothing.
     Enabled: false
 
+  - Id: mod_channel
+    Name: Mods talk to their client plugin over their own packets
+    Description: |
+      A client plugin and the NPC scripts of a mod exchange typed values
+      (numbers, strings, arrays) over two packets of their own, CZ 0x0cfe
+      and ZC 0x0cff, instead of chat lines: modchannel binds a channel to a
+      label, which runs as soon as the packet arrives, also while the player
+      has an NPC dialog open; modsend / modsendto answer. The server sends
+      nothing to a client that did not say hello first, so a client without
+      the plugin never gets a packet it can't read. Off is stock rAthena:
+      the packets are ignored and the commands warn and do nothing.
+    Enabled: false
+    Values:
+      - Key: rate
+        Type: Int
+        Default: 200
+        Min: 10
+        Max: 5000
+        Description: Packets a client may send per second; the rest of that second are dropped.
+      - Key: ask
+        Type: String
+        Default: where mobs scan status buffs
+        Description: |
+          The verbs of channel ask the server answers, by spaces; any other
+          is answered s "off". Empty: none.
+      - Key: protocol
+        Type: Int
+        Default: 2
+        Min: 2
+        Max: 2
+        Description: The wire format's version, for the client's NPC (getextensionvalue); not a setting.
+
 Footer:
   Imports:
     - Path: db/import/extension_db.yml
